# Response headers for the Cantina at salvageunion.io/build (ADR-048).
#
# Copied into `dist/build/` by Vite's publicDir, then moved to `dist/` with its
# `/assets/*` rule scoped to `/build/assets/*` (vite.config.ts), and read by
# Workers Static Assets (ADR-033). It is the app's ONLY source of security
# headers: Static Assets answers every file and every navigation under `/build/`,
# in single-page-application mode, and applies this file to all of them. The
# Worker script runs first for every request (`run_worker_first`) and reads
# those answers through the asset binding, which applies this file too; what it
# builds itself (a missing file's 404, the old host's 301s) runs no script.
#
# robots.txt is srd's (`salvageunion.io/robots.txt`, which allows `/build/`).
# Shared sheets stay crawlable (ADR-032): a link pasted into Discord should
# unfurl and resolve.
#
# `tools/check-observability.ts` requires the CSP here to allow 'self', where the
# browser posts its error reports (`/build/__errors`, src/worker/index.ts);
# tools/smoke-production.sh asserts the CSP and HSTS actually reach the browser.

/*
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Permissions-Policy: geolocation=(), microphone=(), camera=()
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=63072000; includeSubDomains
  X-DNS-Prefetch-Control: on
  # connect-src MUST keep 'self', or the browser blocks every error report
  # before it leaves the page — silent, and it looks healthy (zero errors).
  #
  # The Convex entries fail the same silent way. The accounts client (ADR-030)
  # opens a WebSocket to the deployment for its reactive queries and POSTs
  # mutations over HTTPS, and `@convex-dev/auth` exchanges tokens against the
  # deployment's `.site` origin. Omit them and sign-in never completes, with no
  # error surface. Wildcarded per deployment name because production, a branch
  # deploy and a local `convex dev` differ. Both schemes are required — `wss:`
  # does NOT inherit from `https:`.
  #
  # script-src carries NO 'unsafe-inline': with it, an injected <script>
  # executes. The built `dist/index.html` contains zero inline scripts (Vite
  # bundles every module; the PWA registration is external). If a build ever
  # needs one, give that script a sha256 hash here, the way apps/web does.
  # 'unsafe-inline' stays in style-src deliberately — React's inline `style=`
  # attributes need it, and style injection is not script execution.
  #
  # Cloudflare Web Analytics: the zone's automatic setup injects
  # its beacon into every HTML page at the edge (the page source carries none),
  # loaded from static.cloudflareinsights.com and posting page loads to
  # cloudflareinsights.com; drop either origin and the dashboard silently
  # records nothing.
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self' https://static.cloudflareinsights.com; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; img-src 'self' data: https:; font-src 'self'; connect-src 'self' https://cloudflareinsights.com https://*.convex.cloud wss://*.convex.cloud https://*.convex.site;

# Content-hashed bundle output from Vite's default assetsDir.
#
# Nothing else is marked immutable, and this is the one place this file
# deliberately differs from srd's. cantina's `public/` holds `favicon.svg`,
# `icon-192.png`, `icon-512.png`, `og-image.png` and `logos/` — FIXED names that are mutated in
# place on redesign, so a year of `immutable` would mean a changed icon no
# amount of reloading can dislodge. They, and the shell, keep the platform's
# default `public, max-age=0, must-revalidate`: a stale shell names chunks a
# deploy has rotated away.
/assets/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
